				<wikidot:authorName>Salman Corbette</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>678987</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Even Inuit living in mainly isolated villages have had many of their names anglicized or just plain changed due to the presence of residential schools in the early 1900s. It is entirely plausible to imagine all people involved having &quot;typical&quot; names. First names anyways, the fact that all the last names are anglicized is a bit iffy for me.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
